---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Patio Privacy Planner" description="Plan a patio or balcony with screens on multiple sides, partial walls and railings, and movable furniture.">
<header class="container page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Free planning tool · No account needed</p><h1>Patio Privacy Planner</h1><p class="lead">Start with floor dimensions. Choose walls, railings, and privacy screens, then arrange your furniture.</p></header>
<section class="container section planner-layout">
<form class="panel planner-form" id="privacy-form" novalidate>
<fieldset class="planner-step step-floor"><legend><span>1</span> Floor &amp; roof</legend>
<div class="field-pair"><div><label for="patio-width">Floor width (ft)</label><input id="patio-width" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="1" data-max="100" value="10" required/></div><div><label for="depth">Floor depth (ft)</label><input id="depth" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="2" data-max="100" value="8" required/></div></div>
<label for="space">Space type</label><select id="space"><option value="patio">Patio</option><option value="balcony">Balcony</option></select><p class="small">Both use the same floor geometry. Balcony plans include building, guard, and load checks.</p>
<label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" id="has-roof"/> Roof over the floor</label><div id="roof-fields" hidden><label for="roof-height">Floor to underside of roof (ft)</label><input id="roof-height" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="2" data-max="30" value="8" disabled required/><p class="small">The drawing uses a flat roof over the full floor.</p></div>
</fieldset>
<fieldset class="planner-step step-sides"><legend><span>2</span> Sides &amp; privacy screens</legend>
<p class="small">A is far from you in the drawing, C is nearest. B is right, D is left. Select a screen on every side you want to cover.</p>
<div class="boundary-list"><div class="boundary-row" data-side="back" role="group" aria-label="A · far side">
<div class="boundary-options"><strong>A · far side</strong><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" data-boundary="wall" id="back-wall"/>Wall</label><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" data-boundary="rail" id="back-rail"/>Railing</label><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" data-boundary="screen" id="back-screen" checked/>Screen</label></div><p class="small boundary-hint" hidden>Full wall on this side. Add a railing to describe a wall-and-railing split.</p>
<div class="boundary-mixed" hidden><p class="small">Wall covers the entered section. The rest can have a screen, a railing, or both.</p><div class="field-pair"><div><label for="back-wall-length">A · far side: wall length (ft)</label><input id="back-wall-length" data-auto="true" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.1" data-max="100" value="3" disabled required/></div><div><label for="back-wall-at">Wall position</label><select id="back-wall-at"><option value="start">Wall on left end</option><option value="end">Wall on right end</option></select></div></div><p class="small">A and C run left to right; B and D run far to near.</p></div>
<div class="boundary-screen" >
 <p class="small side-coverage" aria-live="polite"></p>
 <label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" id="back-custom-width"/> Cover only part of this section</label>
 <div class="screen-length" hidden><label for="back-screen-width">A · far side: length to cover (ft)</label><input id="back-screen-width" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.1" data-max="100" value="" disabled required/></div>
 <div class="screen-placement" hidden><label for="back-mode">Screen position on this railing</label><select id="back-mode"><option value="full">Cover the railing and the space above</option><option value="above">Only cover the space above the railing</option></select></div>
 </div>
</div><div class="boundary-row" data-side="right" role="group" aria-label="B · right side">
<div class="boundary-options"><strong>B · right side</strong><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" data-boundary="wall" id="right-wall"/>Wall</label><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" data-boundary="rail" id="right-rail"/>Railing</label><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" data-boundary="screen" id="right-screen" />Screen</label></div><p class="small boundary-hint" hidden>Full wall on this side. Add a railing to describe a wall-and-railing split.</p>
<div class="boundary-mixed" hidden><p class="small">Wall covers the entered section. The rest can have a screen, a railing, or both.</p><div class="field-pair"><div><label for="right-wall-length">B · right side: wall length (ft)</label><input id="right-wall-length" data-auto="true" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.1" data-max="100" value="3" disabled required/></div><div><label for="right-wall-at">Wall position</label><select id="right-wall-at"><option value="start">Wall at far end</option><option value="end">Wall at near end</option></select></div></div><p class="small">A and C run left to right; B and D run far to near.</p></div>
<div class="boundary-screen" hidden>
 <p class="small side-coverage" aria-live="polite"></p>
 <label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" id="right-custom-width"/> Cover only part of this section</label>
 <div class="screen-length" hidden><label for="right-screen-width">B · right side: length to cover (ft)</label><input id="right-screen-width" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.1" data-max="100" value="" disabled required/></div>
 <div class="screen-placement" hidden><label for="right-mode">Screen position on this railing</label><select id="right-mode"><option value="full">Cover the railing and the space above</option><option value="above">Only cover the space above the railing</option></select></div>
 </div>
</div><div class="boundary-row" data-side="front" role="group" aria-label="C · near side">
<div class="boundary-options"><strong>C · near side</strong><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" data-boundary="wall" id="front-wall"/>Wall</label><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" data-boundary="rail" id="front-rail"/>Railing</label><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" data-boundary="screen" id="front-screen" />Screen</label></div><p class="small boundary-hint" hidden>Full wall on this side. Add a railing to describe a wall-and-railing split.</p>
<div class="boundary-mixed" hidden><p class="small">Wall covers the entered section. The rest can have a screen, a railing, or both.</p><div class="field-pair"><div><label for="front-wall-length">C · near side: wall length (ft)</label><input id="front-wall-length" data-auto="true" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.1" data-max="100" value="3" disabled required/></div><div><label for="front-wall-at">Wall position</label><select id="front-wall-at"><option value="start">Wall on left end</option><option value="end">Wall on right end</option></select></div></div><p class="small">A and C run left to right; B and D run far to near.</p></div>
<div class="boundary-screen" hidden>
 <p class="small side-coverage" aria-live="polite"></p>
 <label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" id="front-custom-width"/> Cover only part of this section</label>
 <div class="screen-length" hidden><label for="front-screen-width">C · near side: length to cover (ft)</label><input id="front-screen-width" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.1" data-max="100" value="" disabled required/></div>
 <div class="screen-placement" hidden><label for="front-mode">Screen position on this railing</label><select id="front-mode"><option value="full">Cover the railing and the space above</option><option value="above">Only cover the space above the railing</option></select></div>
 </div>
</div><div class="boundary-row" data-side="left" role="group" aria-label="D · left side">
<div class="boundary-options"><strong>D · left side</strong><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" data-boundary="wall" id="left-wall"/>Wall</label><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" data-boundary="rail" id="left-rail"/>Railing</label><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" data-boundary="screen" id="left-screen" />Screen</label></div><p class="small boundary-hint" hidden>Full wall on this side. Add a railing to describe a wall-and-railing split.</p>
<div class="boundary-mixed" hidden><p class="small">Wall covers the entered section. The rest can have a screen, a railing, or both.</p><div class="field-pair"><div><label for="left-wall-length">D · left side: wall length (ft)</label><input id="left-wall-length" data-auto="true" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.1" data-max="100" value="3" disabled required/></div><div><label for="left-wall-at">Wall position</label><select id="left-wall-at"><option value="start">Wall at far end</option><option value="end">Wall at near end</option></select></div></div><p class="small">A and C run left to right; B and D run far to near.</p></div>
<div class="boundary-screen" hidden>
 <p class="small side-coverage" aria-live="polite"></p>
 <label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" id="left-custom-width"/> Cover only part of this section</label>
 <div class="screen-length" hidden><label for="left-screen-width">D · left side: length to cover (ft)</label><input id="left-screen-width" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.1" data-max="100" value="" disabled required/></div>
 <div class="screen-placement" hidden><label for="left-mode">Screen position on this railing</label><select id="left-mode"><option value="full">Cover the railing and the space above</option><option value="above">Only cover the space above the railing</option></select></div>
 </div>
</div></div>
<div class="field-pair"><div id="wall-fields" hidden><label for="wall-height">Wall height from floor (ft)</label><input id="wall-height" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="1" data-max="30" value="8" disabled required/></div><div id="rail-fields" hidden><label for="rail-height">Railing height from floor (ft)</label><input id="rail-height" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.5" data-max="10" value="3.5" disabled required/></div></div>
<div id="screen-common"><label for="screen-height">How high should the screen reach? (ft above floor)</label><input id="screen-height" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="1" data-max="10" value="6" required/></div><p class="small">Measure from the floor to the top you want, even when screening starts above a railing. A point or comma works for decimals.</p>
<details class="cost-details" id="product-details"><summary>Optional: estimate panels &amp; cost</summary><p class="small">You can draw your space without product measurements. Open this when comparing a specific panel system.</p><label for="panel-width">Usable width of one panel (ft)</label><input id="panel-width" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.1" data-max="100" value="3" disabled required/><label for="module-price">Price per module (USD)</label><input id="module-price" disabled type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0" data-max="100000" placeholder="Leave blank if unknown"/><label for="extra-cost">Additional costs (USD)</label><input id="extra-cost" disabled type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0" data-max="100000" value="0"/><p class="small">Assumes the same unit price on all sides. Add supports, delivery, and taxes yourself.</p></details>
</fieldset>
<fieldset class="planner-step step-furniture"><legend><span>3</span> Furniture &amp; plants</legend><label for="furniture">Start with</label><select id="furniture"><option value="none">No furniture</option><option value="bistro">Two chairs and a table</option><option value="bench">Bench and coffee table</option></select>
<div id="furniture-fields" hidden><div class="field-pair"><div><label for="seat-width">Seat / bench width (ft)</label><input id="seat-width" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.5" data-max="20" value="2" disabled required/></div><div><label for="seat-depth">Seat / bench depth (ft)</label><input id="seat-depth" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.5" data-max="20" value="2" disabled required/></div></div><div class="field-pair"><div><label for="table-width">Table width (ft)</label><input id="table-width" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.5" data-max="20" value="2" disabled required/></div><div><label for="table-depth">Table depth (ft)</label><input id="table-depth" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.5" data-max="20" value="2" disabled required/></div></div><p class="small">After creating the plan, drag individual pieces on the floor. Or focus a piece and use arrow keys. Select a chair to rotate it with the buttons or press R. Heights are illustrative; enter actual floor footprints.</p></div>
<div class="plant-picker"><label for="plant-count">Potted plants</label><select id="plant-count"><option value="0">No plants</option><option value="1">1 plant</option><option value="2">2 plants</option><option value="3">3 plants</option><option value="4">4 plants</option><option value="5">5 plants</option><option value="6">6 plants</option></select><div id="plant-fields" hidden><label for="plant-style">Set all plants to</label><select id="plant-style"><option value="thuja">Small thuja in a pot</option><option value="leafy">Leafy plant in a pot</option></select><div id="plant-choices"></div><div class="field-pair"><div><label for="plant-width">Pot + foliage footprint width (ft)</label><input id="plant-width" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0.5" data-max="5" value="1.5" disabled required/></div><div><label for="plant-height">Total height including pot (ft)</label><input id="plant-height" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="1" data-max="8" value="4" disabled required/></div></div><p class="small">These are illustrative shapes, not plant or growth recommendations. Allow for foliage as well as the pot. Drag each plant in the drawing.</p></div></div>
</fieldset>
<div class="plan-actions"><button class="button" type="submit">Show my layout →</button><button class="reset-button" type="reset">Start over</button></div><p class="small">Your answers stay on this page. Nothing is sent to us or stored automatically.</p><noscript><p>JavaScript is needed for the planner. Read the <a href="/articles/patio-privacy-ideas-for-renters/">patio privacy guide</a>.</p></noscript>
</form>
<section class="panel planner-result" aria-label="Your patio privacy worksheet"><h2>Your space, your layout</h2><p id="planner-state-note" class="small" hidden></p><p id="planner-message" class="form-error" role="alert" tabindex="-1" hidden></p><div id="results" role="region" aria-label="Planner results" aria-live="polite" tabindex="-1"><div class="planner-empty"><p class="eyebrow">Example only · 10 × 8 ft floor</p><div id="planner-preview"></div><h3>Build your layout from the floor up.</h3><p>Start with the floor dimensions. Add walls, railings, and screens on sides A–D, then move furniture into place.</p><p class="small">If a combination does not work, this example or your last valid plan stays visible while you correct it.</p></div></div></section>
</section><section class="container planner-guidance"><h2>What the drawing means</h2><p>A rectangular floor, a flat full-area roof, wall/railing sections on four sides, example screen modules, and furniture/plant footprints. Partial walls can share a side with a privacy screen, railing, or both. Screens cover the entire available section unless you choose a shorter length. Product panel counts are optional and never approve cutting or fitting a panel.</p><p>The planner checks geometric fit and furniture overlap. It does not assess walking clearance, door swings, wind, structural loads, guard compliance, or mounting methods. Confirm product and building requirements before installation. Read our <a href="/articles/patio-privacy-ideas-for-renters/">patio privacy guide</a>.</p></section>
<script type="module" src="/assets/planner.js?v=usability-20261014" is:inline></script></Base>
